; DOMAIN: kato-euler-system [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: Kato's Euler system for the p-adic Galois representation V_p(f) of a newform f attached to E/Q. Beilinson-Kato elements z_Kato(a,b) arise as Steinberg symbols {g_a, g_b} of Siegel units in K_2 of the modular curve Y_1(N), mapped via the etale Chern class / regulator into H^1(Q(mu_m), V_p(f)(1)). These classes are norm-compatible along the cyclotomic tower Q(mu_{mp^n}), satisfying the Euler-factor corestriction relation cor(z_{mp}) = P_p(Frob_p) z_m, hence form an Euler system for V_p(f). Kato's explicit reciprocity law (Theorem 12.5) computes the image of z_Kato under the Perrin-Riou/Coleman big logarithm as the Mazur-Swinnerton-Dyer p-adic L-function L_p(E) (genesis node 137). Kolyvagin's derivative machinery applied to this Euler system bounds the dual Selmer group from above, giving char_Lambda(Sel_dual) | (L_p) — the divisibility half of the Iwasawa Main Conjecture (node 101) — plus finiteness of Sha with the Bloch-Kato bound at finite level and rank-0 BSD (L(E,1) != 0 => E(Q) finite). Bridge: genesis_euler_system (Kolyvagin-derivative/corestriction machinery producing the Selmer upper bound) + genesis_p_adic_l_function_elliptic (image of z_Kato under Coleman map = L_p by the explicit reciprocity law) + genesis_iwasawa_main_conjecture (the divisibility char_Lambda(Sel) | (L_p) is the Euler-system half of IMC) + genesis_bloch_kato (finite-level annihilation of H^1_f giving finite Sha and the Bloch-Kato bound).
(= (kato-class $a $b) (etale-regulator (steinberg-symbol (siegel-unit $a) (siegel-unit $b))))
(= (kato-euler-system $f) (norm-compatible-classes (h1 (cyclotomic-tower) (twist (v-p $f) 1))))
(= (kato-euler-relation $p) (equal (cor $p) (times (euler-factor $p (frob $p)) (kato-base-class))))
(= (explicit-reciprocity $f $p) (equal (coleman-map (kato-class $a $b)) (p-adic-l-function $f $p)))
(= (kato-selmer-bound $f) (divides (char-ideal (selmer-dual $f)) (ideal (p-adic-l-function $f))))
(= (kato-rank-zero-bsd $E) (implies (not-equal (l-value $E 1) 0) (finite (mordell-weil $E))))